            "content": "# PTY Mutex Contention Fix\n\n> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.\n\n**Goal:** Eliminate global mutex contention in `PtyManager` so concurrent sessions don't block each other on every keystroke, resize, or status poll.\n\n**Architecture:** Replace the single `Mutex<HashMap<String, PtySession>>` with `RwLock<HashMap<String, Arc<Mutex<PtySession>>>>`. The outer `RwLock` is held briefly for lookups (read) or insert/remove (write). Per-session `Mutex` isolates each session's I/O. Lock scope in `close()` is minimized so hook cleanup and process teardown don't block the entire manager.\n\n**Tech Stack:** Rust std `RwLock`, `Arc<Mutex<>>`, no new dependencies.\n\n---\n\n### Task 1: Change PtySession storage to per-session Arc<Mutex<>>\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `src-tauri/src/pty_manager.rs:51-53` (PtyManager struct)\n- Modify: `src-tauri/src/pty_manager.rs:56-60` (PtyManager::new)\n\nThis task changes the type signature only. All methods will fail to compile — that's expected. We fix them in subsequent tasks.\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Update the sessions field type**\n\nChange the `PtyManager` struct:\n\n```rust\nuse std::sync::{Arc, Mutex, RwLock};\n\npub struct PtyManager {\n    sessions: Arc<RwLock<HashMap<String, Arc<Mutex<PtySession>>>>>,\n}\n\nimpl PtyManager {\n    pub fn new() -> Self {\n        Self {\n            sessions: Arc::new(RwLock::new(HashMap::new())),\n        }\n    }\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Verify the change compiles in isolation**\n\nRun: `cd src-tauri && cargo check 2>&1 | head -5`\nExpected: Compilation errors in methods that use `self.sessions.lock()` — this is correct. We fix those next.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Commit**\n\n```bash\ngit add src-tauri/src/pty_manager.rs\ngit commit -m \"refactor(pty): change sessions to RwLock<HashMap<String, Arc<Mutex<PtySession>>>>\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### Task 2: Update spawn() to use RwLock write + Arc wrap\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `src-tauri/src/pty_manager.rs:73-284` (spawn method)\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Update the session insertion at the end of spawn()**\n\nFind the block at the end of `spawn()` (around line 278-283):\n\n```rust\n        // Old code:\n        self.sessions\n            .lock()\n            .map_err(|_| AppError::Pty(\"session lock poisoned\".into()))?\n            .insert(session_id.clone(), session);\n```\n\nReplace with:\n\n```rust\n        self.sessions\n            .write()\n            .map_err(|_| AppError::Pty(\"session lock poisoned\".into()))?\n            .insert(session_id.clone(), Arc::new(Mutex::new(session)));\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Verify change compiles (spawn only)**\n\nRun: `cd src-tauri && cargo check 2>&1 | grep \"error\" | head -10`\nExpected: Errors remain in other methods but `spawn()` itself should be clean.\n\n---\n\n### Task 3: Update write() — read-lock map, then lock session\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `src-tauri/src/pty_manager.rs:287-313` (write method)\n\nThe hot path. Previously held the global lock during `write_all()` I/O. Now: brief read-lock to clone the Arc, then per-session lock for the write.\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Rewrite write() with two-phase locking**\n\n```rust\n    pub fn write(&self, session_id: &str, data: &[u8]) -> Result<(), AppError> {\n        let session_arc = {\n            let sessions = self\n                .sessions\n                .read()\n                .map_err(|_| AppError::Pty(\"session lock poisoned\".into()))?;\n\n            Arc::clone(\n                sessions\n                    .get(session_id)\n                    .ok_or_else(|| AppError::Pty(format!(\"session not found: {session_id}\")))?,\n            )\n        };\n        // Map lock is dropped here — other sessions are unblocked.\n\n        let mut session = session_arc\n            .lock()\n            .map_err(|_| AppError::Pty(\"session lock