p \"error\" | head -10`\n\n---\n\n### Task 5: Update get_worktree_id() — read-lock only\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `src-tauri/src/pty_manager.rs:346-356` (get_worktree_id method)\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Rewrite get_worktree_id()**\n\n```rust\n    pub fn get_worktree_id(&self, session_id: &str) -> Result<String, AppError> {\n        let sessions = self\n            .sessions\n            .read()\n            .map_err(|_| AppError::Pty(\"session lock poisoned\".into()))?;\n\n        let session_arc = sessions\n            .get(session_id)\n            .ok_or_else(|| AppError::Pty(format!(\"session not found: {session_id}\")))?;\n\n        let session = session_arc\n            .lock()\n            .map_err(|_| AppError::Pty(\"session lock poisoned\".into()))?;\n\n        Ok(session.worktree_id.clone())\n    }\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Verify compiles**\n\nRun: `cd src-tauri && cargo check 2>&1 | grep \"error\" | head -10`\n\n---\n\n### Task 6: Update close() — minimize lock scope for cleanup\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `src-tauri/src/pty_manager.rs:358-413` (close method)\n\nThis is the critical fix. Previously, hook cleanup (`remove_hooks_config`), SIGTERM, `drop(master)`, and thread spawn all happened while the global lock was held. Now we remove from the map quickly, drop the map lock, then do all cleanup outside.\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Rewrite close() to drop map lock before cleanup**\n\n```rust\n    pub fn close(&self, session_id: &str) -> Result<(), AppError> {\n        let session_arc = {\n            let mut sessions = self\n                .sessions\n                .write()\n                .map_err(|_| AppError::Pty(\"session lock poisoned\".into()))?;\n\n            sessions\n                .remove(session_id)\n                .ok_or_else(|| AppError::Pty(format!(\"session not found: {session_id}\")))?\n        };\n        // Map lock is dropped — other sessions unblocked immediately.\n\n        // Unwrap the Arc<Mutex<PtySession>>. If other references exist\n        // 